<!--
  SIDIS polarized NH3 target (DetElement "Target", plugin SoLID_PolNH3Target).
  Requires from the top level: TargetCenter_z (-350 cm).
  Variant selector: the OPTIONAL constant Target_NH3_Variant (define it in the top-level <define> block; it is
  deliberately not defined here, because a second definition of a constant overrides the first one in DD4hep
  expressions). Undefined -> 1.
    Target_NH3_Variant = 1  SM2023 (default): Scientific-Magnetics split-coil magnet delivered to JLab in 2021, from
                            the JLab target-group CAD (GEMC target/solid_SIDIS_target_NH3_SM, perl 2023-12-14 =
                            __geometry_CAD.txt + the magnet support of __geometry_Original.txt; window half heights
                            from the current perl: entrance 10 cm, exit 22 cm).
                            Vertical Al chamber OD 37.75" (r 47.9425 cm), wall 1", height 34", Al windows 0.2032 mm
                            (+-10 deg) and 0.5 mm (+-28 deg horizontal), 30 K Al shield r 38-39.5 cm with 0.2 mm
                            windows, LHe can r 2.10058 cm, NH3/LHe cup r 1.36144 cm x 2.82702 cm with 17.8 um Al caps,
                            4 Cu coils per side in Al boxes/lids, steel pole rings, Al magnet support with four
                            25 deg cones (+-25 deg openings, preCDR p74).
                        = 2  Oxford2020: 2020 design study used by GEMC solid_SIDIS_NH3_moved_full (chamber r 34 cm,
                            no magnet geometry; the magnet exists only as the oxford_ptarget field map).
  Frames: the part tree origin is the target center (0, 0, TargetCenter_z). The chamber axis is hall y
  (chamber rotation x = -90 deg: local x -> hall x, local y -> hall -z, local z -> hall +y); every inner part
  is positioned in the chamber-vacuum frame exactly like in GEMC. All rotations are ACTIVE,
  R = RotationX(x) * RotationY(y) * RotationZ(z); a GEMC rotation "a b c" is written x=-a y=-b z=-c.
  The <part> trees below were generated from the GEMC txt files (scripts/gen_nh3.py in the work area of the
  implementation; values copied verbatim, cm/deg).
  Not built (deliberate): the GEMC 130 cm air "field" box (it only carries the target field map in GEMC and
  overlaps the NH3 exit pipe), and the study-only W-powder "sheet-of-flame" blocks (not compatible with SM2023).
  Material in the beam (SM2023, upstream->downstream): Al 0.2032 mm, 30K Al 0.2 mm, Al 0.101 mm, LHe 6.86 mm,
  Al 17.8 um, NH3/LHe 28.235 mm, Al 17.8 um, LHe 6.86 mm, Al 0.101 mm, 30K Al 0.2 mm, Al 0.5 mm.
  The 5 T target field is an optional separate fragment: compact/target/field_NH3_target.xml.
-->
